Package: ivamse
Type: Package
Title: IV-LASSO with Approximate-MSE Selection of the Dictionary and Penalty
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-09-04
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yukun", "Ma", role = "aut"),
    person("Manu", "Navjeevan", email = "mnavjeevan@tamu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Bohdan", "Salahub", role = "aut"))
Description: Instrumental variable estimation for linear models in which the
    first stage is fitted by the LASSO, and the dictionary of technical
    instruments and the penalty level are chosen by minimizing a feasible
    estimate of the approximate mean squared error (AMSE) of the resulting
    estimator of the structural coefficient, following Ma, Navjeevan and
    Salahub. First-order asymptotics do not distinguish candidate first stages,
    so the criterion works with second-order terms, trading first-stage
    approximation error against a many-instrument bias whose weight rises with
    the endogeneity of the regressor. The main ivamse() model-fitting function
    provides a formula interface as similar as possible to that of the 'ivreg'
    package, including included exogenous controls, which are partialled out. A
    range of methods is provided for fitted model objects, and 'bread' and
    'estfun' methods make heteroscedasticity-consistent and cluster-robust
    covariances from the 'sandwich' package directly available.
